      "title": "Fill out a Free Application Today!",
      "description": "Careers at GV | Grand View University Warning! Your browser is extremely outdated and not web standards compliant. Your browsing experience would greatly improve by upgrading to a modern browser . Donate Make A Payment Athletics myGVU Contact More Donate Make A Payment Athletics myGVU Contact Search find something... Academics Academic Programs Academic Programs Undergraduate Graduate Programs Online Programs Pre-Professional Preparation Teaching Endorsements Other Programs Other Programs GV Honors Program Center for Mentoring, Coaching & Leadership Development Project Elevate Study Abroad Registrar's Office Registrar's Office Course Catalog Calendars & Schedules Commencement Academic Honors & Awards Dean's & President's List Academic Support Academic Support Academic Learning & Teaching (ALT) Academic Success & Recovery GV Complete Emergency Grant Funds TRIO Student Support Services Library Fill out a Free Application Today! Apply Now Admissions First-Year Students First-Year Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid International Students Iowa Seal of Biliteracy Transfer Students Transfer Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transferring Your Credits International Students Graduate Students Graduate Students Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Grants Admitted Students International Students Graduate Virtual Information Series Online Undergraduate Students Online Undergraduate Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admitted Students Affordability & Financial Aid Affordability & Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Student/Parent Loans Go Private. Pay Public. GV Next Tuition & Fees New Student Orientation Learn everything you need to know about spring orientation at GV. Orientation at GV Student Life Residence Life Residence Life Residency Requirements Housing Options Housing Sign Up Dining Services Wellness Center Campus Involvement Campus Involvement Academic Clubs Campus Clubs & Organizations Student Leadership Campus Ministry Multicultural Community Music Ensembles Viktor the Viking Student Services Student Services Student Health Center Information Technology Accessibility Services Campus Safety & Security Student Counseling Center Life on Campus Explore our traditional, suite, and apartment style housing options. Learn More About About GV About GV Mission, Vision & Values Our History Engagement, Community & Opportunity Fast Facts Our Campus Our Campus Library Bookstore Des Moines + Campus Safety & Security Faculty & Staff Directory Faculty & Staff Directory President Rachelle Keck GV Leadership Board of Trustees Careers at GV Institutional Information Institutional Information Emergency Information Jacobson Institute Institutional Effectiveness Policies & Disclosures Have a Question? Get in touch with us - we are here to help! Contact Us Community & Visitors Des Moines Community Des Moines Community Visit Campus Fine & Performing Arts Employer Partnerships Our Grand Neighborhood GV News Events Conferences & Event Planning Alumni & Donors Alumni & Donors Alumni Awards Stay Connected Alumni Ambassadors Alumni Events Calendar Resources & Transcripts Homecoming at Grand View Parents & Families Parents & Families Make a Payment Athletics Resources Affordability & Financial Aid We'd love to show you around! The best way to get a true feel for campus is to spend some time here. Visit Campus Visit Apply Contact About About GV Our Campus Faculty & Staff Directory President Rachelle Keck GV Leadership Board of Trustees Careers at GV Summary of Benefits Grand View Policies Around Des Moines Contact Us Institutional Information Careers at GV Grand View University is a great place to receive a high quality education, and it's also a great place to work! We are a close-knit community of 250 faculty and staff members enthusiastic about providing the very best education and welcoming new ideas and people into the fold. The average length of employment for our employees is almost 10 years, which is a strong indication that Grand View is the place for a rewarding career. We are committed to attracting, retaining, and rewarding outstanding people. Several strengths that set Grand View University apart include: Strong support for professional growth and development. Belief in a healthy work/life balance, as evidenced in competitive offerings of vacation, sick, and holiday time, as well as standard work week hours of 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. during the academic year and Friday afternoons off during the months of May, June, and July for most of our positions. Exceptional benefits package including health, dental, tuition, and retirement planning. Substantive involvement of faculty and staff in University governance and strategic planning. Located in Des Moines, the vibrant capital city of Iowa. Browse Our Current Available Positions How to Apply Thank you for your interest in Grand View’s current employment opportunities. Grand View accepts applications only for current openings. We do, however, always accept applications for part-time/adjunct faculty. Candidates who wish to apply for an open position should complete the online application process at the end of the desired job posting. Details on what attachments should be submitted with the application are identified in the job posting. Once your application is submitted, you will receive an email confirmation. Our search committee will contact you if additional information is needed. Have a question? Contact the Human Resources department at humanresources @ grandview.edu or 515-263-2842 . About Us Apply Visit Campus Virtual Tour myGVU Parents & Families Alumni Donate to GV Contact Careers at GV Make a Payment The Jacobson Institute 1200 Grandview Ave. Des Moines, IA 50316 ------- (515) 263-2800 (800) 444-6083 © 2026 Grand View University | Privacy Policy Web design by Blue Compass"
    },
    "https://www.grandview.edu/about/directory/careers-at-gv/benefits": {
      "title": "Fill out a Free Application Today!",
      "description": "Summary of Benefits - Careers | Grand View University Warning! Your browser is extremely outdated and not web standards compliant. Your browsing experience would greatly improve by upgrading to a modern browser . Donate Make A Payment Athletics myGVU Contact More Donate Make A Payment Athletics myGVU Contact Search find something... Academics Academic Programs Academic Programs Undergraduate Graduate Programs Online Programs Pre-Professional Preparation Teaching Endorsements Other Programs Other Programs GV Honors Program Center for Mentoring, Coaching & Leadership Development Project Elevate Study Abroad Registrar's Office Registrar's Office Course Catalog Calendars & Schedules Commencement Academic Honors & Awards Dean's & President's List Academic Support Academic Support Academic Learning & Teaching (ALT) Academic Success & Recovery GV Complete Emergency Grant Funds TRIO Student Support Services Library Fill out a Free Application Today! Apply Now Admissions First-Year Students First-Year Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid International Students Iowa Seal of Biliteracy Transfer Students Transfer Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Transferring Your Credits International Students Graduate Students Graduate Students Tuition & Fees Scholarships & Grants Admitted Students International Students Graduate Virtual Information Series Online Undergraduate Students Online Undergraduate Students Application Requirements Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admitted Students Affordability & Financial Aid Affordability & Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Student/Parent Loans Go Private. Pay Public. GV Next Tuition & Fees New Student Orientation Learn everything you need to know about spring orientation at GV. Orientation at GV Student Life Residence Life Residence Life Residency Requirements Housing Options Housing Sign Up Dining Services Wellness Center Campus Involvement Campus Involvement Academic Clubs Campus Clubs & Organizations Student Leadership Campus Ministry Multicultural Community Music Ensembles Viktor the Viking Student Services Student Services Student Health Center Information Technology Accessibility Services Campus Safety & Security Student Counseling Center Life on Campus Explore our traditional, suite, and apartment style housing options. Learn More About About GV About GV Mission, Vision & Values Our History Engagement, Community & Opportunity Fast Facts Our Campus Our Campus Library Bookstore Des Moines + Campus Safety & Security Faculty & Staff Directory Faculty & Staff Directory President Rachelle Keck GV Leadership Board of Trustees Careers at GV Institutional Information Institutional Information Emergency Information Jacobson Institute Institutional Effectiveness Policies & Disclosures Have a Question? Get in touch with us - we are here to help! Contact Us Community & Visitors Des Moines Community Des Moines Community Visit Campus Fine & Performing Arts Employer Partnerships Our Grand Neighborhood GV News Events Conferences & Event Planning Alumni & Donors Alumni & Donors Alumni Awards Stay Connected Alumni Ambassadors Alumni Events Calendar Resources & Transcripts Homecoming at Grand View Parents & Families Parents & Families Make a Payment Athletics Resources Affordability & Financial Aid We'd love to show you around! The best way to get a true feel for campus is to spend some time here. Visit Campus Visit Apply Contact About About GV Our Campus Faculty & Staff Directory President Rachelle Keck GV Leadership Board of Trustees Careers at GV Summary of Benefits Grand View Policies Around Des Moines Contact Us Institutional Information Summary of Benefits Grand View offers a variety of benefits to eligible staff and faculty. Employees working full-time (27 hours or more per week) and part-time (working 18 hours or more per week) on a calendar basis are eligible for benefits. Eligible dependents are an employee’s legal spouse and children. See the list below: (This is a summary of benefits and subject to change without notice. The employee handbook and summary plan documents take precedence for each benefit.) Medical Insurance Employees are offered a choice of three different medical plans through Unity Point Health Partners. Employees and their spouse/dependents are eligible for coverage on the first day of hire. Grand View pays a portion of the premium. Follow this link to access machine-readable files (MRFs) that are made available in response to federal Transparency in Coverage rules. The MRFs contain pricing information about covered items and services, and are formatted to allow third parties to access and analyze the data. Dental Insurance Dental insurance through Delta Dental is available for employees and their spouse/dependents. Coverage begins on the first day of hire. Grand View pays a portion of the premium. Life Insurance Grand View provides one times the employee’s annual salary in life insurance at no cost to the employee. Additional life and AD&D coverage is available for employees, spouses, and dependents who choose to elect the benefit. The voluntary life insurance is paid for by the employee. Disability Insurance Grand View offers both short-term and long-term disability insurance at no cost to employees. This coverage provides 60% of the employee’s salary in the case of an ongoing injury or illness. Flexible Benefit Program The employee’s portion of medical and dental premiums is deducted from paychecks pre-tax. Employees also have the opportunity to participate in medical and/or dependent care flexible benefit programs. Health Savings Account Employees who choose to participate in a qualified High Deductible Health Plan may make contributions to a Health Savings Account in accordance with applicable rules and laws. Employees who elect the HDHP coverage through Grand View will also receive up to $1,000 from the University to be deposited into their health savings account. Discount Vision Care Services Employees are enrolled in discount vision care services upon hire. This program is free for employees and offers discounted fees for exams and products. If desired, employees may elect additional vision care coverage at their cost. 403(B) Retirement Savings Plan Employees may contribute to a 403(b) retirement savings plan upon hire. We also offer a Roth 403(b) option. Money Purchase Plan (MPP) - Principal Financial Group After one year of service, Grand View will contribute 7% of a full-time employee’s monthly salary into the Money Purchase Plan. (One year of service requirement may be waived if an employee has taught or worked full-time in higher education for an equivalent of one year within the past five years.) Voluntary Products We offer a variety of voluntary products through AFLAC should employees desire coverage. This includes hospital, stroke, heart, cancer, and disability policies. Long Term Care Insurance Employees have an option of purchasing long term care insurance through an individual plan. Tuition Waiver Employees are eligible for 100% tuition waiver for undergraduate classes at Grand View. After one year of full-time service, an employee’s spouse and children are eligible for 100% tuition waiver as well for undergraduate classes. In addition, full-time employees may receive a tuition benefit of 80% of tuition for graduate level courses. After one year of employment, an employee’s spouse, and dependent children, up to the age of 26, are eligible to receive a 20% discount on graduate courses at Grand View. Following the one-year anniversary, eligibility begins on the next full-term semester for full-time day or full semester evening students. For students enrolling in only accelerated sessions, eligibility begins on the next subsequent accelerated session. All employees, dependents or graduate assistants who are degree-seeking at Grand View and eligible to file the Free Application for Federal Student Aid must file each academic year they wish to receive GV waiver benefits. Undergraduate students must file by July 1 of each year. This tuition waiver benefit covers tuition only with the responsibility for fees and books being the responsibility of the student. Employee Assistance Program (EAP) This third-party professional assistance is confidential for employees and their dependents. Vacation Time New hires begin accruing vacation upon hire at a rate of 15 days per year. After 5 years of employment, employees earn 20 days per year. Employees with 10 years or more of service earn 26 days per year. While we encourage employees to take time off, vacation balances to a certain amount can be carried over into the next year. Sick Leave Eligible employees earn 1 day of sick leave per month. Holidays We observe the following holidays: New Year’s Day Good Friday Memorial Day Independence Day Labor Day Thanksgiving Day Day after Thanksgiving Christmas Eve Day Christmas Day New Year’s Eve Day Bookstore Employees enjoy a 15% discount on most items in our Bookstore (exclusions: convenience items, software, computers, calculators, class rings, rental textbooks, digital textbooks, textbook access codes). Employees also receive 10% off textbooks. Additional Benefits In addition to the generous traditional benefits provided, Grand View employees also receive some unique added benefits: Hours Standard Hours Academic school year from the first week of August through the spring semester Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Summer Hours Beginning the first week after Commencement (first week of May) through July Monday - Thursday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Friday, 8:00 a.m. - Noon Attire Grand View offers casual business attire and employees are encouraged to wear their Grand View gear on “Wear it Wednesday.” Community Service Leave Staff employees of the University will be granted up to one day of paid leave each calendar year for the pursuit of volunteerism within the local or a neighboring community. Theatre / Sporting Events We have a wonderful fine arts program and offer free seating to staff and faculty. Staff and faculty also receive free admission to most home Grand View sporting events. Go Vikings! Transportation Grand View offers free on-campus parking and a free DART Metro bus pass to employees. On-Site Cafeteria Employees can purchase individual meals or choose from a variety of meal plans to eat at Carlson Commons, our dining center in the Henning Student Center. We also have Einstein Bros Bagels located in our library. Professional Development Opportunities Grand View offers in-house professional development opportunities and encourages employees to take advantage of other industry/job related opportunities for learning. Discount Entertainment Several times a year, Grand View offers discount tickets to staff and faculty for events and locations around Des Moines. Wellness Center All full-time employees and immediate family members have access to the Johnson Wellness Center. Pay Scale Grand View does not publish pay information for faculty and staff. Candidates for employment may inquire about compensation during the interview process. About Us Apply Visit Campus Virtual Tour myGVU Parents & Families Alumni Donate to GV Contact Careers at GV Make a Payment The Jacobson Institute 1200 Grandview Ave. Des Moines, IA 50316 ------- (515) 263-2800 (800) 444-6083 © 2026 Grand View University | Privacy Policy Web design by Blue Compass"
    },
